SUMMARY:[Indigenous Ceremony · Westbank First Nation] Indigenous Veterans 
 Day (Westbank First Nation ceremony: date TBC)
DESCRIPTION:WHEN: Sunday\, November 8\, 2026 (all day / time TBC)\nWHERE: W
 FN Cenotaph\, 1900 Quail Lane\, Westbank\, BC\n\nCATEGORY: Indigenous & Fi
 rst Nations\nTYPE: Indigenous Ceremony\nJURISDICTION: Westbank First Natio
 n\nFEDERAL RIDING: Okanagan Lake West—South Kelowna\nTAGS: Open to Publi
 c\, Free\, WFN Chief & Council\, Veterans\, Reconciliation\, Details TBC\n
 \nABOUT:\nNational Indigenous Veterans Day. Westbank First Nation\, which 
 sits in the heart of the riding\, holds a public ceremony at its cenotaph 
 every year\; in 2025 it was held the Friday before (Nov 7\, 10:30 a.m.–n
 oon\, lunch to follow). Nov 8 2026 is a Sunday\, so check wfn.ca for this 
 year's date. Chief\, council and local elected officials usually attend.\n
 \nWHY IT MATTERS (GOVERNMENT RELATIONS):\nAttending WFN ceremonies builds 
 relationships with WFN leadership\, a self-governing First Nation and a ma
 jor economic player in the riding.\n\nDETAILS:\nOrganizer: Westbank First 
 Nation\nWho attends: WFN Chief and Council\, veterans\, members\, local el
 ected officials\nCost: Free\nAccess: Open to the public\; lunch served aft
 erwards in past years\nContact: WFN Membership Services: membershipservice
 s@wfn.ca\, 250-768-0227\n\nNOT YET CONFIRMED: 2026 date and time not yet p
 ublished by WFN.\n\nSOURCE: https://wfn.ca/blog/Indigenous-Veterans-Day.htm
LOCATION:WFN Cenotaph\, 1900 Quail Lane\, Westbank\, BC
CATEGORIES:Indigenous & First Nations,Indigenous Ceremony,Westbank First Na
 tion,Open to Public,Free,WFN Chief & Council,Veterans,Reconciliation,Detai
 ls TBC
URL:https://wfn.ca/blog/Indigenous-Veterans-Day.htm
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
